    {
      "id": "q5",
      "questionType": "text",
      "question": "How can effective communication break negative feedback loops in change management?",
      "maxScore": 17,
      "timeLimit": 400,
      "correctAnswer": "Effective communication can break negative feedback loops by reducing uncertainty and fear, which are key drivers of resistance. Clear communication about the reasons for change, expected outcomes, and individual impacts helps employees understand the necessity and benefits of change. This understanding reduces resistance, which in turn reduces the need for management pressure, creating a positive feedback loop that supports successful change implementation.",
